{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790283361,"nonce":"P8nXAafCKUtTM87jrV8czljcDDc=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis). Design: doc/design/terminal-renderer.md.\n\n`pick=True` on a list view is gone. It was added the same morning as the way a flow asked a human to choose an issue; the terminal renderer does not implement it and `work.view.list` has no such argument. Every view call returns None today.\n\nSo `flow pick ID` takes its id from the command line, which is what an agent needs and what a human typing a command already has. `flow mine` stays a list of my unstarted and started work, printed; the id comes from reading it.\n\nA flow that wants the human to choose interactively gets that when questions to the user land (choose / confirm / ask / form), which is a deferred view feature, not decided. Until then, choosing is `flow mine`, eyes, and `flow pick ID`.","files":null}]}